    "status": "submitted",
    "answer": "To receive an SBIR award, a company must be a for-profit small business with a U.S. place of business; operate primarily in the United States (or significantly contribute to the U.S. economy); meet applicable U.S. ownership and control rules (normally, more than 50% directly owned and controlled by eligible U.S. citizens/permanent residents and/or qualifying small businesses); and have no more than 500 employees including affiliates. These conditions must be met at the time of award. Certain agencies may have a limited SBIR exception for firms majority-owned by multiple VC, hedge-fund, or private-equity companies.",
